*> Entity packets (docs/protocol 05a 0x01 Add Entity, called Spawn Entity here, and 0x22 Entity
*> Event). The packet id is the caller's. A writer appends nothing and sets PB-ERROR for a value it
*> cannot encode; a reader that fails sets PB-ERROR, leaves PB-POS where it was and yields zeros.
*> Spawn Entity uses the record PB-SPAWN of copy/PBENT.cpy.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. PB-PUT-SPAWN-ENTITY.
*> USING PB-BUFFER, PB-SPAWN: entity id VarInt, UUID, entity type VarInt, X, Y and Z Doubles, the
*> movement as an LpVec3 (00 §4.6), pitch, yaw and head yaw as Angles (00 §4.4), data VarInt. A
*> negative entity id or entity type is an error, found before anything is written.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY PBENT.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING PB-BUFFER PB-SPAWN.
     IF PB-SP-ENTITY < 0 OR PB-SP-TYPE < 0
         MOVE 1 TO PB-ERROR
         GOBACK
     END-IF
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-ENTITY
     CALL "PB-PUT-UUID" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-UUID
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-TYPE
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-X
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-Y
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-Z
     CALL "PB-PUT-LPVEC3" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-MOVE-X PB-SP-MOVE-Y PB-SP-MOVE-Z
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-PITCH
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-YAW
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-HEAD-YAW
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-DATA
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM PB-PUT-SPAWN-ENTITY.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. PB-GET-SPAWN-ENTITY.
*> USING PB-BUFFER, PB-SPAWN out. A negative entity id or entity type is an error.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-START               BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY PBENT.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING PB-BUFFER PB-SPAWN.
     MOVE PB-POS TO WS-START
     CALL "PB-GET-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-ENTITY
     CALL "PB-GET-UUID" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-UUID
     CALL "PB-GET-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-TYPE
     CALL "PB-GET-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-X
     CALL "PB-GET-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-Y
     CALL "PB-GET-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-Z
     CALL "PB-GET-LPVEC3" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-MOVE-X PB-SP-MOVE-Y PB-SP-MOVE-Z
     CALL "PB-GET-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-PITCH
     CALL "PB-GET-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-YAW
     CALL "PB-GET-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-HEAD-YAW
     CALL "PB-GET-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SP-DATA
     IF PB-SP-ENTITY < 0 OR PB-SP-TYPE < 0
         MOVE 1 TO PB-ERROR
     END-IF
     IF PB-ERROR = 1
         MOVE WS-START TO PB-POS
         INITIALIZE PB-SPAWN
     END-IF
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM PB-GET-SPAWN-ENTITY.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. PB-PUT-ENTITY-EVENT.
*> USING PB-BUFFER, entity id, event id (both BINARY-LONG): the entity id as a fixed 4-byte Int (not
*> a VarInt), the event id as a Byte. An event id outside -128 to 127 is an error.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 L-ENTITY               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-EVENT                BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING PB-BUFFER L-ENTITY L-EVENT.
     IF L-EVENT < -128 OR L-EVENT > 127
         MOVE 1 TO PB-ERROR
         GOBACK
     END-IF
     CALL "PB-PUT-INT" USING PB-BUFFER L-ENTITY
     CALL "PB-PUT-BYTE" USING PB-BUFFER L-EVENT
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM PB-PUT-ENTITY-EVENT.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. PB-GET-ENTITY-EVENT.
*> USING PB-BUFFER, entity id out, event id out (BINARY-LONG; the event id is signed, -128 to 127).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-START               BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 L-ENTITY               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-EVENT                BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING PB-BUFFER L-ENTITY L-EVENT.
     MOVE PB-POS TO WS-START
     CALL "PB-GET-INT" USING PB-BUFFER L-ENTITY
     CALL "PB-GET-BYTE" USING PB-BUFFER L-EVENT
     IF PB-ERROR = 1
         MOVE WS-START TO PB-POS
         MOVE 0 TO L-ENTITY L-EVENT
     END-IF
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM PB-GET-ENTITY-EVENT.
